---
import { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';
import { roundedContributions, switchingConstraintBounds } from '../../public/scripts/participation-calibrated-swing.js';
const { names } = Astro.props as { names: Record<string, string> };
type DriverRow = { id: string; state_code: string; office: string; components_pp: Record<string, number>;
	reported_comparison: { baseline_year?: number; reported_change_pp: number | null;
		other_and_unallocated_pp: number | null; baseline_alignment_pp: number | null } };
const data = JSON.parse(readFileSync('data/participation-return-attribution/20261110-02/viewer-data.json', 'utf8'));
const calibration = JSON.parse(readFileSync('data/participation-return-attribution/20261111-03/return-constrained-viewer.json', 'utf8'));
type CalibratedRow = { id: string; state_code: string; office: string;
	point: { reported_change_pp: number; components_pp: Record<string, number> } | null };
const receipt = JSON.parse(readFileSync('data/participation-return-attribution/20261110-02/download.json', 'utf8'));
const payload = JSON.stringify({ data, calibration, names }).replaceAll('<', '\\u003c');
const pp = (value: number | null) => value === null ? 'Unavailable' : `${value > 0 ? '+' : ''}${value.toFixed(2)}`;
---
<section id="participation-return-drivers" class="participation-current" aria-labelledby="return-drivers-title">
	<header class="section-intro">
		<p class="kicker">2026 · Swing and transition scenarios</p>
		<h2 id="return-drivers-title">Swing, switching and participation</h2>
		<p>Explore the <strong>reported swing</strong> and fitted transition scenarios on one map.
			Each scenario is constrained to both elections, not independently measured voter histories.</p>
	</header>
	<p class="caption">Reported swing compares earlier <strong>same-office returns</strong>.
		Known-D/R margin = 100 × (D − R) / (D + R). Gray is unavailable.
		Assumptions and ranges remain below the map.</p>
	<div class="driver-controls">
		<label>2026 office<select data-driver-office disabled><option value="house">House · states</option>
			<option value="senate">Senate</option><option value="governor">Governor · frames</option></select></label>
		<label>Map view<select data-driver-view disabled>
			<option value="reported_total">Reported swing</option>
			<option value="switching">Switching · fitted</option>
			<option value="modeled_nonparticipation">No contest vote · fitted</option>
			<option value="entry">Entry / return · fitted</option>
			<option value="other_choice">Other-party choice · fitted</option>
			<optgroup label="Original survey-frame demographic scenarios · not return-fitted">
				<option value="scenario_retaining">Keep party choice · scenario</option>
				<option value="scenario_switching">Switch party choice · scenario</option>
				<option value="scenario_nonparticipation">Nonparticipation · scenario</option>
			</optgroup>
		</select></label>
		<label data-driver-group-control hidden>Source group<select data-driver-group disabled>
			<option value="">Overall source frame</option>
		</select></label>
		<label class="driver-state-control">State<select data-driver-state disabled><option value="">Loading state context…</option></select></label>
	</div>
	<p data-driver-status class="caption" role="status">Saved return-constrained scenarios; original unfitted source estimates remain archived below.</p>
	<div data-driver-summary class="driver-summary" hidden aria-live="polite"></div>
	<div class="driver-maps">
		<section class="driver-map-card" aria-labelledby="driver-map-title">
			<h3 id="driver-map-title" data-driver-map-title>Reported swing</h3>
			<p class="caption" data-driver-map-caption>Total same-office change in the known-D/R margin.</p>
			<div class="driver-map" data-driver-map="reported_total"></div>
		</section>
	</div>
	<div class="driver-map-key" aria-label="Shared signed margin-point scale">
		<div><div class="driver-map-ramp"></div><div class="driver-map-ticks">
			<span data-driver-scale-min></span><span>0</span><span data-driver-scale-max></span>
		</div><div class="driver-map-directions"><span>Republican direction</span><span>Democratic direction</span></div></div>
		<span class="driver-no-model"><i></i>No qualified comparison / model</span>
	</div>
	<p class="caption driver-map-note">Colour shows <strong>signed percentage-point changes or contributions to the margin</strong>,
		not party vote shares or turnout rates. In each fitted scenario, reported total =
		party-choice switching + no current-contest vote + entry/return + Other-party choice.
		The common accounting-frame size and transitions are modeled, not measured people.
		No state estimate is spread onto counties or precincts.</p>
	<details class="explorer-notes"><summary>Selected state: fitted contributions and assumption ranges</summary>
		<div data-driver-detail class="driver-detail" hidden></div>
	</details>
	<details class="explorer-notes"><summary>How to read these estimates and their uncertainty</summary>
	<p class="caption">Nine scenarios vary prior persistence from half to double and the assumed
		common accounting-frame size from 0.8× to 1.25×. Their ranges are
		<strong>assumption sensitivity, not confidence or identification intervals</strong>.
		Each scenario has a nonnegative transition table constrained to both return endpoints.
		Shapley averaging includes denominator effects in the four mechanisms rather than
		adding an unmodeled residual. Displayed equation terms use sum-preserving rounding.</p>
	<p class="caption">The original survey-derived synthetic transitions are a prior only.
		Recalled presidential choice is not substituted for the previous same-office result.
		The synthetic accounting frame is not a measured eligible population; outside the
		target contest does not identify no ballot, new eligibility, death, migration or first-ever voting.
		Unreported Other-party totals remain unknown in the source and are explicitly prior-assumed
		in the scenario, never filled as observed zeros. No state model is allocated to counties or precincts.</p>
	<p class="caption">Aggregate totals leave many possible transition tables. In all 89 comparable
		central frames, <strong>zero D↔R switching is compatible with the same totals</strong>.
		The selected-state details report its sharp gross-switching feasibility range, not a margin
		contribution or confidence interval. A separate complete constraint-only analysis includes every
		witness table; it does not refit the transition model or convert missing Other into nonvote.</p>
	<p class="caption">The separate party-choice scenarios simulate gross shares within recalled major-party
		choices, not contributions to the electoral swing. Their half/double persistence envelopes are
		assumption sensitivity, not confidence intervals. Gross-switching state-held-out error is 1.39 pp;
		House-model transport to Senate/governor and demographic party associations remain unvalidated.
		Historical voting marginals do not identify individual staying-home or switching histories.</p>
	</details>
	<details class="explorer-notes"><summary>Every saved return-constrained scenario</summary>
		<div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="All 113 return-constrained decisions">
			<table><caption>Central fitted scenario; not independently observed voter histories. The final column is a compatible gross-switching percentage of previous D/R votes, not margin points or a confidence interval. Unavailable is not zero.</caption>
				<thead><tr><th scope="col">State / office</th><th scope="col">Reported swing</th>
					<th scope="col">Switching</th><th scope="col">No contest vote</th>
					<th scope="col">Entry / return</th><th scope="col">Other-party choice</th>
					<th scope="col">Compatible gross switching</th></tr></thead>
				<tbody>{calibration.rows.map((row: CalibratedRow) => {
					const rounded = row.point ? roundedContributions(row.point) : null;
					const compatible = switchingConstraintBounds(row);
					return <tr data-saved-calibrated={row.id}><th scope="row">{names[row.state_code]} · {row.office}</th>
						<td class="numeric">{pp(row.point?.reported_change_pp ?? null)}</td>
						{['switching', 'nonparticipation', 'entry', 'other_choice'].map(key =>
							<td class="numeric">{pp(rounded?.[key] ?? null)}</td>)}
						<td class="numeric" data-saved-switching-bounds={row.id}>{compatible
							? `${compatible.minimumPercent.toFixed(1)}% to ${compatible.maximumPercent.toFixed(1)}%`
							: 'Unavailable'}</td></tr>;
				})}</tbody>
			</table>
		</div>
	</details>
	<details class="explorer-notes"><summary>Archived original survey-frame estimates · not the fitted swing scenarios</summary>
		<div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="All 113 saved modeled effect estimates">
			<table><caption>Archived unfitted survey-frame terms, not a decomposition of the reported same-office swing. Unavailable is not zero.</caption>
				<thead><tr><th scope="col">State / office</th><th scope="col">Switching</th><th scope="col">Nonparticipation</th>
					<th scope="col">Entry</th><th scope="col">Other</th><th scope="col">Unknown</th>
					<th scope="col">Denominator</th><th scope="col">Current-frame gap</th>
					<th scope="col">Prior-office year</th><th scope="col">Reported swing</th>
					<th scope="col">Other / unallocated total</th><th scope="col">Baseline alignment</th></tr></thead>
				<tbody>{data.rows.map((row: DriverRow) =>
					<tr data-saved-driver={row.id}><th scope="row">{names[row.state_code]} · {row.office}</th>
						{['switching', 'modeled_nonparticipation', 'no_prior_contest_vote_entry',
							'other_choice', 'unresolved', 'denominator', 'return_frame_gap'].map(key =>
							<td class="numeric">{pp(row.components_pp[key])}</td>)}
						<td>{row.reported_comparison.baseline_year ?? 'Unavailable'}</td>
						{['reported_change_pp', 'other_and_unallocated_pp', 'baseline_alignment_pp'].map(key =>
							<td class="numeric">{pp(row.reported_comparison[key as 'reported_change_pp'])}</td>)}</tr>)}</tbody>
			</table>
		</div>
	</details>
	<div class="download-links"><a href={receipt.url}>Complete historical returns, inputs, all models/scenarios, code and checksums · ZIP</a></div>
	<div class="download-links"><a href="https://github.com/hanshanley/margin_of_error/releases/download/participation-return-constrained-20261111-01/complete-analysis.zip">Complete return-constrained model, all 801 scenarios and transition cells, inputs, code and checksums · ZIP</a></div>
	<div class="download-links"><a href="https://github.com/hanshanley/margin_of_error/releases/download/participation-flow-identification-20261111-01/complete-analysis.zip">Complete compatible-flow bounds, all 3,824 extremal tables, original inputs, code and checksums · ZIP</a></div>
	<div class="download-links"><a href="https://github.com/hanshanley/margin_of_error/releases/download/participation-transition-simulation-20261111-01/complete-analysis.zip">Complete conditional transition simulations, every input/query/seed, code and checksums · ZIP</a></div>
	<script type="application/json" is:inline data-driver-data set:html={payload}></script>
</section>
<script>
	import { initializeReturnDrivers } from '../../public/scripts/participation-return-drivers.js';
	initializeReturnDrivers();
</script>
<style>
	#participation-return-drivers { min-width: 0; margin-block: 1.5rem 2rem; }
	.driver-controls { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));
		gap: .75rem; margin-block: 1.25rem .75rem; max-width: 55rem; }
	.driver-controls label { display: grid; min-width: 0; gap: .3rem; font: .73rem var(--sans); }
	.driver-controls label[hidden] { display: none; }
	.driver-controls[data-scenarios="true"] { grid-template-columns: repeat(4,minmax(0,1fr)); max-width: 65rem; }
	.driver-controls :is(select,input) { width: 100%; min-width: 0; padding: .5rem; border: 1px solid var(--rule);
		background: var(--paper); color: var(--ink); font: inherit; }
	.driver-maps { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0,1fr); margin-top: 1.5rem; }
	.driver-map-card { min-width: 0; }
	.driver-map-card h3 { margin: 0 0 .35rem; font: 400 1.3rem var(--serif); }
	.driver-map-card > p { margin: 0 0 .5rem; }
	.driver-map { min-height: 120px; }
	.driver-map :global(svg) { display: block; width: 100%; max-width: 62.5rem; height: auto; margin-inline: auto; }
	.driver-map :global(.driver-state) { stroke: var(--paper); stroke-width: .8; vector-effect: non-scaling-stroke; cursor: pointer; }
	.driver-map :global(.driver-state:hover), .driver-map :global(.driver-state.selected) { stroke: #243f49; stroke-width: 1.8; }
	.driver-map :global(.driver-inset-label) { fill: var(--muted); font: 15px var(--sans); }
	.driver-map-key { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
		gap: .5rem .75rem; font: .66rem/1.4 var(--sans); color: var(--muted); margin-block: .75rem; }
	.driver-map-key > div { width: min(100%, 20rem); }
	.driver-map-ramp { height: .5rem; background: linear-gradient(to right,#a47045,#f1eee6,#2c6c75); }
	.driver-map-ticks { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; margin-top: .25rem; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
	.driver-map-directions { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; margin-top: .25rem; }
	.driver-no-model { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: .35rem; margin-left: .5rem; }
	.driver-no-model i { width: .65rem; height: .65rem; background: #d6d3cb; }
	.driver-map-note { max-width: 85ch; margin-inline: auto; }
	.driver-detail { margin-top: 1rem; padding-top: .5rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); min-width: 0; }
	.driver-summary { margin-block: 1rem; padding-block: .75rem; border-block: 1px solid var(--rule); }
	.driver-summary :global(h3) { margin: 0 0 .4rem; font: 400 1.15rem var(--serif); }
	.driver-summary :global(p) { margin: .4rem 0; }
	.driver-summary :global(.driver-equation) { font: .85rem/1.65 var(--sans); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
	@media(max-width:760px) {
		.driver-controls { grid-template-columns: repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr)); }
		.driver-controls[data-scenarios="true"] { grid-template-columns: repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr)); }
		.driver-state-control { grid-column: 1 / -1; }
		.driver-controls[data-scenarios="true"] .driver-state-control { grid-column: auto; }
		.driver-map-key { justify-content: flex-start; }
		.driver-map-key > div { width: 100%; }
		.driver-no-model { flex-basis: 100%; margin-left: 0; }
	}
</style>
